{
  "format": "read-round/1",
  "description": "One read round of one endpoint's meters, as a collector makes it, under the profiles in contract/profiles and the policy here (retries: further attempts after a failed one; busy_backoff_ms: the wait before each retry after exception 05 or 06). Per meter, in order: its identity, in the requests and with the fallback of identity-checks.v1.json, judged as there; then, if it passed, each of its profile's registers, in profile order. steps: each request the collector must make, as [unit_id, table, address, count], its attempt (from 1) and the wait before it in ms, then what came of it: words (the reply), an exception code, failed (a transport failure: timeout, closed, malformed_response and the like), or unreachable (no connection could be opened, so nothing was sent; its value is the socket error). Exception 0A or 0B misses the meter at once. 05 or 06 is retried after busy_backoff_ms, up to retries, then misses the meter. Any other exception misses that read alone, with no retry. A transport failure is retried at once, up to retries, then misses the meter. Unreachable misses the meter at once, and every later meter in the round is not tried. A meter missed counts its attempts on the register it stopped at, 0 on every later one; a meter whose identity check failed or did not match is missed in full with 0 attempts. events: each reading and missed read, in the order made, in batch.v1's fields (timestamps and the endpoint left out). Every implementation that reads meters must make each request and record each event.",
  "policy": {
    "retries": 2,
    "busy_backoff_ms": 30
  },
